index 0000000..c9648f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/notes/followups/w50-b.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# Task: daemon-side `shell.exec` and quick `exec` commands for attached clients (W50-b, D-16.1094) Phase: follow-up (P17 attach) Owner: builder w50b
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-23). The daemon serves `shell.exec` and runs quick `exec` commands for an attached
+client through `service/host_shell.py`, the one definition `--local` now uses too. Outside the
+task's own files: `tooling/checks/security_allow.json` (the `shell` exception moved with the code),
+threat model B-SHELL-1 / B-DAEMON-5 proofs, and three wave-48 contract tests that pinned the old
+refusal (`test_ws_tui_session.py`, `test_ws_pickers.py`, `test_ws_tui_reads.py`). Generated files
+(`packages/protocol/src/generated/*`, `field_docs.json`, `protocol.md`) were regenerated with the
+repo's tools after the last hand edit to `protocol/bridge.py`; regenerate again after merging
+slice [a]. D-ids for W50-b-1 .. 4 and the D-16.1094 text update are for the integrator.
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): `tui_gateway/methods_tools.py`
+(`shell.exec` near the end; `_dispatch_quick`, the quick `exec` stage of `command.dispatch`), for
+behaviour only. Ours: `tui_bridge/methods_shell.py`, `tui_bridge/methods_slash.py`
+(`BridgeSlashHost.run_quick`), `service/slash_commands.py`, `service/daemon_slash.py`,
+`service/picker_reads.py`, `service/path_completion.py` (`session_folder`), `gateway/ws/methods.py`,
+`protocol/bridge.py` (`ShellExecParams`, the method rows), `safety/child_env.py`, threat model rows
+B-SHELL-1 and B-DAEMON-5, `docs/notes/P17/ws-endpoint.md` (wave 48 h), LEAD-NOTES wave 48 / 49.
+Evidence: none (our own attach path; the in-process bridge is the spec).
+
+What it does (own words): an attached TUI talks to the daemon over its WebSocket. Its `!command`
+(and `{!command}` inside a prompt) calls `shell.exec`, which the daemon did not serve (`-32601`);
+quick commands of type `exec` were refused by the daemon (W48-h-2) and marked `unavailable` in its
+catalogue, so they were not offered. Now the daemon serves `shell.exec` and runs quick `exec`
+commands with exactly the rules `--local` uses: the same dangerous-command detection (a hardline or
+dangerous command is refused with `SHELL_REFUSED`, no approval card: the agent is the place for
+those; a detector that cannot load refuses), the environment from the one builder
+(`safety.child_env`, the connection's profile scope, provider keys out, the session's pins), stdin
+from the null device, its own process group, the 30 s limit on the scope's clock (`SHELL_TIMEOUT`),
+redaction before the tail cut (4 000 / 2 000 characters). The command runs in the session's folder
+when it names one, else the profile's `terminal.cwd`, else the daemon's own folder (the same order
+as the bridge, where the last step is the bridge's folder). A named session must be one this
+connection attached (B-DAEMON-5): another connection's session reads `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`.
+
+Inputs → outputs: `shell.exec {command, session_id?}` → `{stdout, stderr, code}` or `TEXT_EMPTY`,
+`SHELL_REFUSED`, `SHELL_TIMEOUT`, `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`; `command.dispatch` of a quick `exec` name →
+`{kind: exec, output}` (output and `(exit N)` as in `--local`); `commands.catalog` lists quick
+`exec` commands `server` (no longer `unavailable`) and `complete.slash` offers them.
+
+Files: `src/indus/service/host_shell.py` (new: the checks, runner and clean-up written once),
+`src/indus/tui_bridge/methods_shell.py` (the bridge's handler over it), `src/indus/service/daemon_slash.py`
+(`run_quick`, no refusal), `src/indus/service/picker_reads.py` (`DAEMON_QUICK_EXEC` gone),
+`src/indus/gateway/ws/methods.py` (`shell.exec`, quick `exec` offered), `src/indus/protocol/bridge.py`
+(`shell.exec` row gains `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`; `ShellExecParams.session_id` doc), generated
+`packages/protocol/src/generated/*`, `src/indus/protocol/field_docs.json`,
+`docs/user/reference/protocol.md`; tests below; threat model B-SHELL-1 / B-DAEMON-5 proofs.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- empty or blank command → `TEXT_EMPTY` (path `command`) before anything runs;
+- hardline / dangerous → `SHELL_REFUSED` with the reason; detector import or check failure → refused;
+- environment builder failure → `SHELL_REFUSED`, nothing runs;
+- a command that never ends → killed (process group) at the limit, `SHELL_TIMEOUT "stopped after 30 s"`;
+- huge output → only the redacted tail; a token crossing the cut never survives as halves;
+- a foreign or unknown session id → `SESSION_NOT_FOUND` (never runs in another viewer's folder);
+- a session whose folder vanished → falls back to `terminal.cwd`, then the daemon's folder;
+- quick `exec` command with an empty `command` → `TEXT_EMPTY`, as in `--local`;
+- Windows: the runner already uses `shell=True` and `proc.kill()` off POSIX (unchanged code moved).
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- W50-b-1: one definition (`service/host_shell.py`) for both hosts; the gateway may not import
+  `tui_bridge`, so the bridge's handler now delegates to the service module (no behaviour change).
+- W50-b-2: the daemon serves `shell.exec` to any connection that passed the ticket check (every
+  attached client is the owner, B-DAEMON-2), with no rule looser than `--local`; a named session is
+  checked against the connection's attachments like every other session-addressed call.
+- W50-b-3: the folder order is the bridge's (session folder, `terminal.cwd`, the host process's
+  folder); on the daemon the last step is the daemon's folder, which is also where the agent's own
+  local terminal runs for a session with no folder.
+- W50-b-4: protocol: `shell.exec` declares `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`; quick `exec` commands are no longer
+  `unavailable` on the daemon (`DAEMON_QUICK_EXEC` removed, W48-h-2's quick `exec` part closed).
+- Not taken: an approval card for a dangerous `!command` (the reference and `--local` refuse; a
+  card would be a new path); running through the profile's sandbox backend (the bridge runs the
+  owner's own command on the host, B-SHELL-1; the daemon does the same).
+
+Tests we will write:
+- contract (`tests/contract/gateway/test_ws_shell.py`): refused / empty commands over the socket,
+  both streams and exit code equal to `--local`'s for the same command, the session's folder is
+  the working folder, a foreign session `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`, the timeout on the scope clock, the
+  redacted tail, provider keys absent from the child env, quick `exec` through `command.dispatch`
+  equal to `--local`'s and listed `server` / offered by completion;
+- unit (`tests/unit/service/test_host_shell.py`): the shared runner's folder order and refusals;
+- updated: `test_ws_tui_session.py` (the quick `exec` command is no longer refused or unavailable),
+  `test_ws_pickers.py` (the daemon's slash completion now equals `--local`'s exactly),
+  `test_ws_tui_reads.py` (only `DAEMON_REFUSED` is `unavailable` in the daemon's catalogue).
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- W50-b-1 .. W50-b-4 above (D-ids to be given at integration).
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened `tui_gateway/methods_tools.py`):
+- [x] empty command refused (test: `test_ws_shell.py::test_refused_and_empty_commands_match_local`)
+- [x] hardline / dangerous refused, "use the agent" wording kept in our own words (same test)
+- [x] detector not importable → refused, nothing runs (test: `test_host_shell.py::test_a_detector_that_cannot_load_refuses`)
+- [x] sanitised env (no provider keys) (test: `test_ws_shell.py::test_the_child_env_has_no_provider_keys`)
+- [x] redact before the tail cut, 4 000 / 2 000 (test: `test_ws_shell.py::test_long_output_keeps_the_redacted_tail`)
+- [x] 30 s timeout (test: `test_ws_shell.py::test_a_command_is_stopped_at_the_limit_on_the_scope_clock`)
+- [x] quick `exec`: output joined, non-zero exit shown, a dangerous one refused (test: `test_ws_shell.py::test_quick_exec_commands_run_on_the_daemon_as_in_local`)
+- [x] env builder failure refuses, nothing runs (test: `test_host_shell.py::test_an_environment_that_cannot_be_built_refuses`)
+- [x] gap found: the reference has no session check (no daemon) — ours refuses a foreign session, pinned by `test_ws_shell.py::test_a_session_another_connection_attached_reads_as_unknown`
+- Deliberate differences: the reference's quick `exec` answers an error for a non-zero exit and
+  cuts the head of the output; ours (since P12) shows the output with `(exit N)` and keeps the
+  redacted tail, on both hosts. The reference runs `shell.exec` in the server's folder; ours runs
+  in the session's folder first. The reference has no daemon; the attachment check is ours.
+- Not taken: see above.
